From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: preserve routing for an Alt Mode partner

The connector-status bitmap conversion changed the USB-only partner check
into a USB-bit check. A partner advertising both USB and Alt Mode therefore
receives a generic USB-mode write after its Alt Mode handler programs DP.

On Uke, PAN sets DP pin D and UCSI then reports partner_flags=3 before
ucsi_partner_change overwrites the route with TYPEC_STATE_USB. Leave that
route to its Alt Mode handler. Keep normal USB, USB4, accessory modes, data
roles, PD and disconnect cleanup unchanged.

Fixes: 226ff2e681d0 ("usb: typec: ucsi: Convert connector specific commands to bitmaps")

--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -1356,7 +1356,8 @@
 			typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_MODE_AUDIO);
 			break;
 		default:
-			if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB))
+			if (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB) &&
+			    !UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_ALT_MODE))
 				typec_set_mode(con->port, TYPEC_STATE_USB);
 		}
 
